ications."},{"question":"What are pull-up resistors, and why are they important for I2C communication?","answer":"Pull-up resistors are electrical components that pull the voltage on a line to a high logic level when no active device is driving it low. In I2C, both SDA and SCL lines are open-drain, meaning devices can only pull them low. Pull-up resistors are essential to bring the lines back to a high state, enabling proper signal transmission."},{"question":"What is a baud rate, and why is it important in serial communication?","answer":"Baud rate is the rate at which symbols (bits in simple cases) are transmitted over a communication channel. It is crucial in serial communication because both the transmitting and receiving devices must operate at the same baud rate to correctly interpret the transmitted data."},{"question":"How can you debug issues with I2C communication?","answer":"Common debugging steps include checking wiring, verifying the correct I2C address (often found using an I2C scanner sketch), ensuring pull-up resistors are present, checking power supply, and using a logic analyzer to observe SDA/SCL signals."},{"question":"Name two wireless communication protocols commonly used in IoT and their typical applications.","answer":"1. **Wi-Fi**: High bandwidth, good for local internet connectivity, e.g., smart home devices, surveillance cameras. 2. **Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE)**: Low power, short-range, good for connecting wearables, sensors to smartphones."},{"question":"What are the advantages of using an I2C LCD module over a parallel LCD module?","answer":"An I2C LCD module requires only 2 data pins (SDA, SCL) from the microcontroller, saving valuable GPIO pins, whereas a parallel LCD module typically requires 6 to 11 pins. This simplifies wiring and makes it easier to add more peripherals."},{"question":"When would `Serial.readStringUntil('\n')` be useful?","answer":"This function is useful for reading entire lines of text from the serial buffer until a newline character is encountered. It's often used when receiving commands or configuration settings sent from a user via the Serial Monitor or from another device."}],"bloomsTaxonomy":"K3 - Apply","coMapping":"CO4","precautions":"1. Ensure the correct I2C address is used for the LCD module (commonly 0x27 or 0x3F).
