times using an I2C scanner sketch."},{"question":"How often should you read from a DHT11 or DHT22 sensor?","answer":"DHT11 and DHT22 sensors are relatively slow. DHT11 typically requires a minimum of 1 second between readings, and DHT22 requires at least 2 seconds. Reading faster than this can result in invalid data or sensor damage."},{"question":"What are the components of the `LiquidCrystal_I2C` object initialization `lcd(0x27, 16, 2)`?","answer":"`0x27` is the I2C address of the LCD module. `16` indicates the number of columns (characters per line), and `2` indicates the number of rows (lines) on the LCD."},{"question":"What is the purpose of the pull-up resistor on the DHT sensor's data line?","answer":"The DHT sensor uses a single-wire bi-directional communication protocol. The data line is an open-drain output on the DHT. The pull-up resistor ensures that the line is pulled HIGH when the sensor is not actively pulling it LOW, providing a defined logic state and proper signal integrity."},{"question":"How can you debug an I2C LCD that isn't displaying anything?","answer":"Debugging steps include: checking wiring (VCC, GND, SDA, SCL), verifying the correct I2C address using an I2C scanner sketch, ensuring the `lcd.init()` and `lcd.backlight()` calls are present, and checking for power to the LCD."},{"question":"What other types of sensors could be easily integrated into this setup and displayed on the LCD?","answer":"Other digital or analog sensors could be integrated, such as a photoresistor (LDR) for light intensity, a potentiometer for analog input, or a soil moisture sensor. Many I2C sensors (e.g., BMP280 for pressure/temperature) could also be added easily due to the shared I2C bus."},{"question":"How would you display longer text strings that exceed the 16-character limit of a single LCD line?","answer":"For longer strings, you can use `lcd.setCursor()` to move the text to the second line. Alternatively, for very long text, you might implement horizontal scrolling by repeatedly shifting the text on the display, or use a larger display like a graphical LCD or OLED."}],"bloomsTaxonomy":"K3 - Apply","coMapping":"CO4","precautions":"1. Ensure the DHT sensor is correctly wired, including the pull-up resistor on its data line, as specified by the sensor's datasheet.
