4. **Hardware Setup (Raspberry Pi - Alternative):**
    *   Power up your Raspberry Pi.
    *   Connect the long leg (anode) of the LED to a GPIO pin (e.g., GPIO 17, physical pin 11) via a 220 Ohm resistor. Connect the short leg (cathode) to a GND pin (e.g., physical pin 9).
    *   Connect the positive (+) pin of the active buzzer module to another GPIO pin (e.g., GPIO 27, physical pin 13). Connect the negative (-) pin to a GND pin.
