 allows multiple I2C devices to share the same two lines."},{"question":"How do you find the I2C address of an LCD module?","answer":"The I2C address of an LCD module can be found by running an I2C scanner sketch (available online) on the microcontroller. Common addresses are `0x27` or `0x3F`, but it can vary based on the PCF8574 chip configuration."},{"question":"What is the role of the `lcd.init()` and `lcd.backlight()` functions in `LiquidCrystal_I2C` library?","answer":"`lcd.init()` initializes the LCD module and its I2C expander chip, preparing it for receiving commands and data. `lcd.backlight()` turns on the backlight of the LCD screen, making the display visible."},{"question":"Why is it important to include `delay()` between DHT sensor readings?","answer":"DHT sensors are relatively slow and require a certain minimum time (typically 1-2 seconds) between readings to stabilize and provide accurate data. Reading too frequently can lead to erroneous or failed readings."},{"question":"What does `isnan(h)` check for, and why is it important when reading DHT data?","answer":"`isnan(h)` checks if the value of `h` (humidity) is 'Not a Number'. This check is crucial because DHT sensors can sometimes fail to read data due to timing issues or sensor malfunction, returning invalid values. Checking for `isnan` allows the program to handle these errors gracefully."},{"question":"How do you display special characters like the degree symbol on an LCD?","answer":"Special characters like the degree symbol (`°`) can be displayed by sending their ASCII or custom character code. For many LCDs, `(char)223` (or `0xDF`) represents the degree symbol."},{"question":"Can multiple I2C devices share the same SDA and SCL pins?","answer":"Yes, multiple I2C devices can share the same SDA and SCL pins. Each I2C device has a unique 7-bit address, which the master (microcontroller) uses to select and communicate with a specific slave device on the bus."},{"question":"What are some common applications where a local temperature/humidity display is useful?","answer":"Local temperature/humidity displays are useful in home weather stations, incubators, greenhouses, server rooms, smart thermostats, and industrial environmental monitoring where immediate, on-site feedback is desired."}],"bloomsTaxonomy":"K3 - Apply","coMapping":"CO4","precautions":"1. Ensure the DHT sensor's data line has a 10k Ohm pull-up resistor (if not already integrated into the module) to ensure stable communication.
